spans.s:
√lubh (lúbhyati; lulóbha, lulubhé;
lubdhá; lóbdhum). --1. go astray;
 —2.
be lustful; have strong desire; lubdha,
longing for. [cf. ἡ λίψ, *λιφ-ς, ‘longing’;
λίπ-τ-ομαι, ‘long for’; Lat. lub-et, lib-et,
‘is desired or agreeable’; libens, ‘willing,
glad’; libīdo, ‘desire’; AS. leōf, ‘dear,’
Eng. lief, ‘dear, gladly’; Ger. lieb, ‘dear’;
also Eng. love.]
